    "title": "When will April Social Security payments arrive? See the schedule",
    "text": "April 1, 2026, 10:03 a.m. ETSocial Security benefits for April 2026 will be paid on Wednesdays, starting April 8, based on the recipient's birth date.Supplemental Security Income (SSI) payments for April will be issued on Wednesday, April 1.Nearly 71 million Americans receive Social Security, with over five million recipients in Florida alone.New month, new round of Social Security benefits.The Social Security Administration typically pays benefits on Wednesdays, with the first wave scheduled for April 8, according to the SSA’s calendar.In Florida, more than five million people rely on Social Security payments every month, according to Congressional Statistics from December 2024. Nearly 71 million Americans receive Social Security, and 7.4 million receive SSI, according to January 2026 data from the Social Security Administration.Nearly 1 in 5 Florida retirees, family members, veterans and others receive Social Security benefits, according to the AARP.Here's what to know about this year's Social Security benefits.Social Security payment schedule for April 2026The Social Security Administration’s 2026 distribution schedule is available online for recipients to use for budgeting.Regular Social Security retirement benefits are slated to be distributed on the SSA’s usual schedule based on birth date:Wednesday, April 8: Birth dates between the first and 10th of the month.Wednesday, April 15: Birth dates between the 11th and 20th of the month.Wednesday, April 22: Birth dates between the 21st and 31st of the month.Those who began getting benefits before May 1997 will be paid on Friday, April 3.When do SSI checks go out in April?Recipients of Supplemental Security Income checks will be issued their April payments today, Wednesday, April 1.What is SSI?Supplemental Security Income provides monthly benefits to those with limited income or resources who are 65 or older, blind, or have a qualifying disability. Children with a qualifying disability can also get SSI, according to the SSA's website.Adults who qualify for SSI generally do not have monthly wages above $2,073.Those eligible for SSI can begin the application process online, in person at your local Social Security office or by calling 1-800-772-1213 (TTY 1-800-325-0778) from 8 a.m. to 7 p.m. local time during the work week.SSI payment schedule for 2026SSI checks will be sent out on the following dates in 2026, according to the SSA calendar:Wednesday, April 1, 2026: April 2026 paymentFriday, May 1, 2026: May 2026 paymentMonday, June 1, 2026: June 2026 paymentWednesday, July 1, 2026: July 2026 paymentFriday, July 31, 2026: August 2026 paymentTuesday, Sept. 1, 2026: September 2026 paymentThursday, Oct. 1, 2026: October 2026 paymentFriday, Oct. 30, 2026: November 2026 paymentTuesday, Dec. 1, 2026: December 2026 paymentWhat do I do if my scheduled payment date passes without payment?The Social Security Administration suggests that if you don’t receive your payment on the expected date, allow three additional mailing days before contacting the agency. Most will arrive on time because 99% of beneficiaries are paid electronically.Where is a Social Security office in Florida?There are 54 Social Security offices throughout Florida, from Pensacola to Key West. To locate one near you, check here.When can you start collecting Social Security?Everyone can start receiving reduced Social Security benefits as early as age 62. However, waiting until full retirement age results in a larger monthly payment. That age has gradually increased in recent years, rising by two months for each successive birth year.You can calculate your full retirement age on the SSA website.Samantha Neely is a trending reporter for the USA TODAY NETWORK-Florida, covering pop culture, theme parks, breaking news and more. You can get all of Florida’s best content directly in your inbox each weekday by signing up for the free newsletter, Florida TODAY, at https://floridatoday.com/newsletters.",
